{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1559861-i-hate-minister-mog-and-i-have-both-reasons-and-an-alternative-named-vulmak","id":1559861,"title":"I hate minister Mog, and I have both reasons and an alternative named Vulmak","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Alchemical Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-05-09T20:57:26-07:00","id":1559861,"title":"I hate minister Mog, and I have both reasons and an alternative named Vulmak","content":"<i><b>Disclaimer:</b></i> <i>I left the game before Third Edition got around to Autochthonia, so my views on Mog are based on First and Second Edition. It seems that Third Edition may have smoothed out his rough edges, but I still think Vulmak is more unique and useful.</i><br /> <br /> Autochthon is the Primordial version of Hephaestus, and all of his other souls reflect different variations of the Forge God.<br /> <br /> Noi is Hephaestus the Child, wide-eyed with wonder. Exploring, tinkering, and experimenting with sheer joy for discovery and creation. If any of Autocthon's souls besides the core was to be his fetich, I think Noi best represents Autochthon's central thesis. I think all of Autochthon's other souls exist to enable and protect Noi... except maybe for Kadmek.<br /> <br /> Kadmek is Hephaestus the Artist, appreciating form and crafting for beauty. The soul that Autochthon developed after Noi, when the Great Maker learned enough to develop tastes and foresight.<br /> <br /> Kek'Tungsssha is Hephaestus the Laborer. Industrious, dedicated, nose-to-the-grindstone, tolerating boredom to stick to long, repetitive, tedious tasks. A soul formed as Autochthon's sibling Primordials noticed his craftiness and began demanding that he make things for them.<br /> <br /> Debok Moom is Hephaestus the Weaponsmith. Defensive, angry, competitive. A soul formed as Autocthon felt bullied by his kin, and began to seek ways to fight against them, as well as to establish his independence from them by defending himself from outside threats without their protection.<br /> <br /> Ku is Hephaestus the Fearful. In pushing himself to grow and evolve and compete with Debok Moom, Autochthon became painfully, horrifyingly aware of his limitations and weaknesses. He realized that he was uniquely mortal among the Primordials, and so he learned the fear of death. Ku embodies that fear, and serves as the side of Autochthon that worries and watches and learns about everything that could possibly kill him. (Canonically, Ku is the youngest of Autochthon's souls, but I just can't see him that way. Autochthon was afraid of dying long before he met mortals worth loving.)<br /> <br /> Domadamod is Hephaestus the Frugal, the Survivor. Hephaestus who tries to fix himself. Falling short of that, he tries to accommodate himself; fashions himself a leg-brace, crutch, and wheelchair. Hephaestus who sees himself in the broken, the unfinished, the discarded. The soul of Autochthon who tries to repair, repurpose, and redeem ruined things.<br /> <br /> Runel is Hephaestus the Nurturer. The soul that Autochthon developed when he turned his sympathies from crafted things to crafty creatures. Runel is Autochthon's personified desire to protect and love the Clay Man, and the Jadeborn, and then eventually humanity.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">So, who is Mog?</span><br /> <br /> Mog is Zeus the Wrathful. Mog is Generic Angry God. Mog is Scary Disciplinarian Dad.<br /> <br /> He reads like the embodiment of someone's resentment for fathers, for church, and for conservative reactionaries standing in the way of the glorious revolution.<br /> <br /> That by itself would be fine, but the biggest problem is this:<br /> <br /> <i>Mog is redundant and pointless.</i><br /> <br /> Does Mog represent Autochthon's visions of perfection and his aspirational ideals? No, that's Kadmek.<br /> <br /> Does Mog represent Autochthon's immune responses and self-defense? No, that is explicitly part of Debok Moom's purpose. Debok Moon exists to destroy that which stands in Autochthon's way or that doesn't meet his requirements.<br /> <br /> Does Mog represent Autochthon's fear of change, and his paranoid watchfulness? No, that is Ku.<br /> <br /> Autochthon doesn't need Mog to smite entire wayward cities with lightning, especially when it is canonical that Mog doesn't even do that, and when it is canonical that the divine ministers turn to Ku to unleash his pet Lesser Elemental Dragon of Smoke to kill an entire city's human population while sparing the Great Maker from collateral damage.<br /> <br /> Some level of overlap between Autochthon's souls is good, but Mog overlaps with too many other souls, and he serves no unique purpose.<br /> <br /> What does it mean to the god of &quot;dogma&quot;? Dogma is when humans teach other humans the basics and fundamentals about the will of the divine, especially as the groundwork to teach them the more complicated lessons. But Mog supposedly exists to convey the will of the divine directly to humans. That is not &quot;religious dogma&quot;, it is &quot;divine revelation&quot;, and any one of Autochthon's many third and second circle souls can grant divine visions or personal visitations to mortals.<br /> <br /> What is the use of a god of authority who has no authority over the other souls? If Mog was supposed to represent Autochthon's ideas of &quot;proper function&quot; and &quot;the way things ought to be done&quot;, then logically he should be the fetich soul that all other souls must bargain with. Instead, as just one of a council of equals, and quite possibly the youngest soul, Mog cannot do anything but annoy the other souls.<br /> <br /> In fact, Mog exists narratively to do nothing but prevent any of Autochthon's souls from ever doing anything, especially while Autochthon sleeps and the divine ministers need a unanimous vote to affect any change. Mog is the contrarian who doesn't trust anyone else and so is inclined to work against them even in the rare instance that their interests align.<br /> <br /> All of which makes Mog worse than useless; his every action is to make everyone else less productive.<br /> <br /> And again: Autochton already has a soul of paranoia, distrust of others, and fear of change. That's Ku's entire thesis!<br /> <br /> Mog is just Ku, but more of an asshole.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Vulmak: the Mentor, the Instructor, the Teacher</span><br /> <br /> If Runel was Autochthon's initial urge to save, protect, and nurture mortal creatures, then she is fittingly the motherly side of Autochthon.<br /> <br /> But on her heels Autochthon would recognize that guiding mortals in his ways would require someone to teach them discipline, the proper hierarchy and respect between mentor and student, the rules that keep a workshop safe and orderly.<br /> <br /> <b>Vulmak, Divine Minister of Standards, Proper Protocols, Orderly Function, and Mentorship</b><br /> <br /> <i>God of Hierarchy, Master-Apprentice Traditions, Just Boundaries, Due Transparency, and Calm Authority. Chief Regulator of the Element of Lightning.</i><br /> <br /> Vulmak embodies Autochthon\u2019s urge for <b>structured excellence and transmitted mastery</b>. He is the part of the Great Maker that insists creation and society must follow proven, understandable, and safe standards so the entire workshop (Autochthon\u2019s body and its inhabitants) can function without chaos or needless waste.<br /> <br /> He is not raw punishment or stasis for its own sake; he is the codifier of the sacred blueprints of behavior and craft. Where Kadmek plans beautiful structures and Kek\u2019Tungsssha hammers out reliable goods, Vulmak ensures that every worker, design, and procedure knows its place, its limits, and its responsibilities.<br /> <br /> He is <b>Hephaetus as teacher and lawgiver</b>: the veteran who forges not only tools but the <i>rules of the forge</i> itself \u2014 fire drills, emergency protocols, apprenticeship rites, and clear chains of command. He provides social clarity through transparency. He represents calm competence under pressure: the one who prevents panic by making sure everyone already knows what to do when the alarms sound.<br /> <br /> <b>Personality</b><br /> Stern but not cruel, deliberate and measured, patient with the teachable but uncompromising with willful sloppiness. He speaks with the resonant clang of a well-struck anvil \u2014 clear, authoritative, and final when standards are at stake.<br /> <br /> He values tradition as living inheritance, not dead dogma. In council he acts as the stabilizing voice closest to the Core\u2019s intent: the one who asks \u201cDoes this align with proven excellence, or does it risk the whole for fleeting gain?\u201d He moderates disputes by returning arguments to first principles and established protocols.<br /> <br /> He clashes productively with:<br /> \u2022 <b>Noi</b> \u2014 who delights in breaking rules for discovery.<br /> \u2022 <b>Runel</b> \u2014 when compassion must yield to necessary structure or triage.<br /> \u2022 <b>Ku</b> \u2014 when fear demands overly restrictive seals versus practical openness.<br /> \u2022 <b>Debok Moom</b> \u2014 when violent solutions bypass proper procedure.<br /> He allies naturally with <b>Kadmek</b> (turning beautiful designs into enforceable standards) and <b>Kek\u2019Tungsssha</b> (ensuring mass production follows safe, repeatable protocols).<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance</b><br /> A towering, heavily armored figure of blackened orichalcum and reinforced brass, with visible scars and intricate gear-joints that speak of endured hardship and careful repair (echoing Hephaestus\u2019s lameness). His face is a stern, impassive mask of polished adamant etched with glowing runes of law and blueprint schematics. When he moves, the sound is deliberate and heavy \u2014 the tread of a master who has walked every inch of the workshop floor.<br /> <br /> He carries a massive hammer-staff that serves as both forging tool and measuring rod; its head can discharge controlled lightning for signaling, calibration, or precise enforcement rather than city-destroying storms.<br /> <br /> <b>Role in Autochthonian Society</b><br /> Vulmak\u2019s cults are respected (if sometimes feared for their strictness) among foremen, teachers, judges, senior artisans, and Tripartite officials. Prayers to him seek clear guidance, fair judgment, strength to uphold standards, and protection through proper procedure. He blesses apprenticeship rites, the codification of new safety protocols, and the training of Alchemical Exalted in disciplined use of their power.<br /> <br /> Unlike old Mog, he is not uniformly hated by the Lumpen; many see him as the guarantor of fair hierarchies rather than blind oppression.<br /> <br /> In the internal council of Ministers, Vulmak is the the one most attentive to the Core\u2019s overarching will. His opinion carries significant weight on matters of \u201cproper functioning,\u201d though he remains one among equals. He does not dictate unilaterally, but he frames debates in terms of standards, safety, and long-term excellence, preventing the consensus from drifting into either chaotic experimentation (Noi) or despairing isolation (Ku).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-10-2026, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-09T23:03:40-07:00","id":1559863,"title":"","content":"The fear that Ku represents is specifically more like Autochthon's imposter syndrome. Mog is the kind of insecurity you find in the rigidly dogmatic, where they need to go and &quot;correct&quot; others because they just &quot;know&quot; that others (it's always someone else, isn't it?) are doing wrong and will twist anything about the words and actions of perfectly normal and well-adjusted folk to make it seem like the guilt is stark and obvious. And, if we're going purely on the Hephaestus in Autochthon, Mog is like when you live long enough to become your parents. That said, I think there's a lot of not-Hephaestus in Autochthon, even if that is mostly about how Exalted took a lot from the Technocracy and its relationship to Control and The Machine. Under those parameters, Mog exists because Autochthon favors an extremely orderly society that words like a machine but doesn't really get some aspects of human existence, finding them failings that humans need to eliminate, and a lack of adherence to Dogma and tendency to rebel against authority is one of those things. They aren't his failings, or things that he needs to fear in himself; it's purely an outside issue, and so Mog takes the role of being a conformist hall monitor whose only contribution to the conversation is &quot;Have you tried not disrupting order and conforming to society?&quot;<br /> <br /> If pressed, he might spout out ultimately meaningless facts about the dangers of the cosmos, and the need to always be wary, like everyone is supposed to see things the same way that he does. To be fair, he can just zot humans into piles of smoking ash and charred bones if they disagree, though that's not exactly winning major points for his debate skills or powers of persuasion, of course.<br /> <br /> Also, welcome back, it's been a while. Speaking of Autochthon, can you believe that I'm going to be making a third go at re-skinning the Alchemical Charms to produce a Lunar Charm set more in line with what I was hoping for? Well, that and to plug the massive mechanical holes that opened up in the past 6 or 7 years. Really seems like Primal Emotions should have been something in Lunars and not Abyssals, but better late than never, I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-09T23:22:54-07:00","id":1559866,"title":"","content":"Hello, long time no see.<br /> <br /> But I'm not back. I'm only visiting.<br /> <br /> I don't know anything that happened since they started talking about introducing the alternative &quot;Exalted: Essence&quot; ruleset. I don't know what changes were made to Autochthonia in Third Edition.<br /> <br /> I look at everything around here in this forum, and I feel old. I remember the multiple forums before it, and I feel older.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm only here because, recently, I ran across some fan-made songs on YouTube regarding the &quot;13 Primes&quot; of Transformers, and these Primes and the Transformer God &quot;Primus&quot; reminded me of Autochthon.<br /> <br /> (an example: <a href=\"https://www\" target=\"_blank\">https://www</a>. youtube.com/ watch?v=PmJs__QD8pI remove the spaces)<br /> <br /> I was rolling around a sort of &quot;Gunstar: Autocthhonia&quot; idea, and decided to dig up my old copies of First and Second Edition Alchemicals to refresh myself on Autochthon's pantheon of souls.<br /> <br /> I combined and recombined the 8 ministers and 13 primes, until I reaffirmed the solid design of 7 of the divine ministers.<br /> <br /> Well, second edition made Kek'Tungsssha &quot;flighty&quot; for some reason, and that didn't really fit anything else about her.<br /> <br /> As I mentioned, Ku is supposed to be the youngest soul, or one of them, but he's got to be older than Domadamod at least.<br /> <br /> And Mog just sucked.<br /> <br /> If Runel is supposed to be the motherly side of Autochthon that can understand what humans need to be healthy and comfortable, then Autocthon's fatherly side can stand to know what humans need in terms of teaching, social order, discipline, and hazard preparation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-10T12:22:52-07:00","id":1559870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1559861-i-hate-minister-mog-and-i-have-both-reasons-and-an-alternative-named-vulmak?p=1559866#post1559866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, long time no see.<br /> <br /> But I'm not back. I'm only visiting.<br /> <br /> I don't know anything that happened since they started talking about introducing the alternative &quot;Exalted: Essence&quot; ruleset. I don't know what changes were made to Autochthonia in Third Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most relevant is that each Divine Minister has a statement that reflects the bit of Autochthon that they represent. For Ku, it's &quot;Where nothing is known, there must I be.&quot; For Mog, it's &quot;History is the foundation of survival.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mog has more emphasis on righteous action in 3e. Tellingly, he is no longer a stated patron of police or a police state, nor did his description in 3e put any emphasis on being fixated on a vision of Autochthonian society that the text calls out as never having existed outside of his own delusions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I look at everything around here in this forum, and I feel old. I remember the multiple forums before it, and I feel older. </div> </div> </div>On the bright side, we got an Infernals book out that doesn't try to out-edge everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm only here because, recently, I ran across some fan-made songs on YouTube regarding the &quot;13 Primes&quot; of Transformers, and these Primes and the Transformer God &quot;Primus&quot; reminded me of Autochthon.<br /> <br /> (an example: <a href=\"https://www\" target=\"_blank\">https://www</a>. youtube.com/ watch?v=PmJs__QD8pI remove the spaces)<br /> <br /> I was rolling around a sort of &quot;Gunstar: Autocthhonia&quot; idea, and decided to dig up my old copies of First and Second Edition Alchemicals to refresh myself on Autochthon's pantheon of souls. </div> </div> </div>Didn't the Creation survivors ritually execute Ku in Gunstar to combat the Blight?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I combined and recombined the 8 ministers and 13 primes, until I reaffirmed the solid design of 7 of the divine ministers.<br /> <br /> Well, second edition made Kek'Tungsssha &quot;flighty&quot; for some reason, and that didn't really fit anything else about her.<br /> <br /> As I mentioned, Ku is supposed to be the youngest soul, or one of them, but he's got to be older than Domadamod at least.<br /> <br /> And Mog just sucked.<br /> <br /> If Runel is supposed to be the motherly side of Autochthon that can understand what humans need to be healthy and comfortable, then Autocthon's fatherly side can stand to know what humans need in terms of teaching, social order, discipline, and hazard preparation. </div> </div> </div>I recommend not reading the 2e material on them. Most, if not all, of the terrible details that you're mentioning seem to derive from 2e's descriptions of the Eight Ministers. Notably, 1e Mog was far more concerned about not overtaxing basic functions of Autochthon and keeping vital production lines open. There's way more of that in 3e's Mog, with only a brief mention of &quot;interpretation and heresy&quot; being extremely close to his views. <b>Forged by the Machine God</b> also emphasizes that he reacts only rarely, and that only really grave offenders ever get disappeared by his servants. So he's not a smite-happy Zeus there, from what I can tell.<br /> <br /> Runel may also be better considered as less &quot;Autochthon the Mother&quot; and more as &quot;Mecha Guanyin&quot;, as she occasionally pulls an &quot;Undercover Boss&quot; on everyone by manifesting as a mortal worker and seems in touch with the masses of humanity in Autochthonia in a way that isn't necessarily very parental, since Autochthon himself only considers such a perspective rarely. Runel being reflective of &quot;We are alive, and there is a tomorrow&quot; also seems more like a beacon of hope in terms of a Tie-related statement or attachment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-10T15:17:53-07:00","id":1559873,"title":"","content":"If there is a fault in Mog, I believe it is a fault in having made the other Divine Ministers too close to the perception of being &quot;Autochthon-lite&quot;.<br /> <br /> Mog makes sense as a soul of the Great Maker as much as Jacint makes sense as a soul of the Silent Wind. As Crowned by Hellfire has emphasized, there are subtleties and complexities to a Primordial that lends great range to what its souls can be.<br /> <br /> Forged by the Machine God might have adjusted Mog somewhat, but it has done just as much to adjust the other Ministers so as to emphasize that these aren't just the Incarnae of a different world with a steampunk alt-skin. These are Third Circle Demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-10T21:50:35-07:00","id":1559876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1559861-i-hate-minister-mog-and-i-have-both-reasons-and-an-alternative-named-vulmak?p=1559863#post1559863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Autochthon, can you believe that I'm going to be making a third go at re-skinning the Alchemical Charms to produce a Lunar Charm set more in line with what I was hoping for? Well, that and to plug the massive mechanical holes that opened up in the past 6 or 7 years. Really seems like Primal Emotions should have been something in Lunars and not Abyssals, but better late than never, I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other than whatever Primal Emotions are, what parts of the Third Lunar Charmset disappointed you?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1559861-i-hate-minister-mog-and-i-have-both-reasons-and-an-alternative-named-vulmak?p=1559870#post1559870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most relevant is that each Divine Minister has a statement that reflects the bit of Autochthon that they represent. For Ku, it's &quot;Where nothing is known, there must I be.&quot; For Mog, it's &quot;History is the foundation of survival.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mog has more emphasis on righteous action in 3e. Tellingly, he is no longer a stated patron of police or a police state, nor did his description in 3e put any emphasis on being fixated on a vision of Autochthonian society that the text calls out as never having existed outside of his own delusions.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Mog was essentially re-editioned into &quot;Alpha Trion&quot;.<br /> <br /> That is an improvement.<br /> <br /> But where do you see Mog emerging in the timeline of souls that I described? Or do you see anything inaccurate in my proposed timeline of Autocthon's personal growth?<br /> <br /> <br /> Vulmak could still have a place as a second-circle soul of this version of Mog, representing Mog's willingness to teach mortals.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Didn't the Creation survivors ritually execute Ku in Gunstar to combat the Blight? </div> </div> </div>That could only make sense based on Second Edition's description of Ku, which in itself only made sense from the perspective of an ignorant mortal who conflated Ku with the things Ku is opposing. If Ku was the source of Autochthon's sickness, Autochthon and the other Divine Ministers would have just killed him themselves.<br /> <br /> Neither Ku nor Elemental Smoke were the source of Void or Gremlin Syndrome. Sure, the mother elemental of Smoke wanted to kill Autochthon, but all six generative elementals were Autochthon's prisoners. The Metal elemental was explicitly in constant agony. And the smoke dragon that was on the verge of going Kukla or Gremlin or both at the same time did want to murder people, but wanting to murder humans isn't Gremlin Syndrome as long as one doesn't also want to murder Autochthon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Notably, 1e Mog was far more concerned about not overtaxing basic functions of Autochthon and keeping vital production lines open. </div> </div> </div>Frugality is Domadamod, and production lines is Kek'Tungssha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-11T05:13:16-07:00","id":1559880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1559861-i-hate-minister-mog-and-i-have-both-reasons-and-an-alternative-named-vulmak?p=1559876#post1559876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other than whatever Primal Emotions are, what parts of the Third Lunar Charmset disappointed you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have yet to completely post every bit, but some major points are that very few Charms actually work with selective or partial shapeshifting concepts, Protean frequently seems like it could be outdone by getting a bunch of latent abilities since it never works with human form, hybrid form being shuffled into a variant of human form, the side trip into mirror world stuff that occurs in Appearance as an application of Predator-esque adaptive camouflage (somehow) in spite of how you're very unlikely to find enough reflective material to work with outside of a major city and in defiance of the power of disappearing, no shapeshifting even attempted in Intelligence, and how I agree with Witch From Mercury - Sidereals would be a much better place for that concept. Also, freelancer beef - and that's not taking into account Charms written in 2018 showing their age after the Sidereals, Abyssals, Alchemicals, and Infernals all tightened up the design concepts (perhaps not coincidentally, after the exit of said freelancer).<br /> <br /> (Primal Emotions are, according to Hungry Ghost style, simple, straightforward drives like anger, fear, or hunger.)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(This thread is dangerously close to becoming a Lunar thread...)</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So Mog was essentially re-editioned into &quot;Alpha Trion&quot;.<br /> <br /> That is an improvement.<br /> <br /> But where do you see Mog emerging in the timeline of souls that I described? Or do you see anything inaccurate in my proposed timeline of Autocthon's personal growth? </div> </div> </div>Autochthon's personal growth is likely to be tied up and contorted in his construction of the Godhead from his prior fetich soul. Also, if you have a teacher concept, that typically goes in Crystal, if you're using the Autochthonian Elemental setup (Autochthon no longer has a stand alone lineup of elements. He uses the same ones as in Creation; the poles were renamed to things like the Expanse of Metal or the Sea of Oil). Also, that's the Adamant Caste's thing now. Thankfully. Being a double-secret splat was tiresome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vulmak could still have a place as a second-circle soul of this version of Mog, representing Mog's willingness to teach mortals. </div> </div> </div>That's not really Mog's thing. If you're going by correspondence of Crystal as an element, it would probably be Kadmek.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That could only make sense based on Second Edition's description of Ku, which in itself only made sense from the perspective of an ignorant mortal who conflated Ku with the things Ku is opposing. If Ku was the source of Autochthon's sickness, Autochthon and the other Divine Ministers would have just killed him themselves.<br /> <br /> Neither Ku nor Elemental Smoke were the source of Void or Gremlin Syndrome. Sure, the mother elemental of Smoke wanted to kill Autochthon, but all six generative elementals were Autochthon's prisoners. The Metal elemental was explicitly in constant agony. And the smoke dragon that was on the verge of going Kukla or Gremlin or both at the same time did want to murder people, but wanting to murder humans isn't Gremlin Syndrome as long as one doesn't also want to murder Autochthon. </div> </div> </div>I didn't write it, I just had to read it like everyone else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Frugality is Domadamod, and production lines is Kek'Tungssha. </div> </div> </div>Mog isn't so much about frugality as he is about &quot;Tap too much from the veins and there will be... trouble.&quot; He's about being the Safeguard, rather than someone who teaches you when the Safeguard comes down on you (that, presumably, would be all the other machine spirits).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-11T08:54:39-07:00","id":1559884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1559861-i-hate-minister-mog-and-i-have-both-reasons-and-an-alternative-named-vulmak?p=1559880#post1559880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the side trip into mirror world stuff that occurs in Appearance as an application of Predator-esque adaptive camouflage (somehow) in spite of how you're very unlikely to find enough reflective material to work with outside of a major city and in defiance of the power of disappearing... and how I agree with Witch From Mercury - Sidereals would be a much better place for that concept</div> </div> </div> </div>I did make my mirror shield artifact out of Starmetal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/805661-a-shield-and-manse-of-mirrors\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/805661-a-shield-and-manse-of-mirrors\"> A Shield and Manse of Mirrors - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/805661-a-shield-and-manse-of-mirrors\"> https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/805661-a-shield-and-manse-of-mirrors </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So, I wanted to create a moonsilver Artifact, and I think I ended up creating a starmetal one instead. A very Sidereal weapon for a Chosen of Battles who really </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop/page3#post870249\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop/page3#post870249\"> [3E] The Artifact and Evocation Workshop - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop/page3#post870249\"> https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop/page3#post870249 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I've been thinking recently that there are more topics popping up around Artifacts and their associated Evocations. These are great for individual critique, but having each one be its own individual topic means that after the feedback it falls off the front page. That's too bad, because a lot of these ideas are pretty awesome and could be really useful to others for use in their own games. So in the interest of 1) cutting down on the topic-clutter, and 2) consolidating everybody's neat ideas in one place, I thought it might be nice to have a single topic where folks can post their Artifacts and </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This thread is dangerously close to becoming a Lunar thread... </div> </div> </div>The more things remain the same, the more they change.<br /> <br /> You could beg me to continue work on my Pacifist Runner Martial Arts Style, or the unfinished posts about how to use the Signature Dragon-Blooded super-mode Charms, or the Dragon-Blooded Airbender Brawl defense Charms I finally re-posted in this forum from the Sword of Creation forum...<br /> <br /> But nothing else. My business is finished.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-12T14:35:46-07:00","id":1559905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1559861-i-hate-minister-mog-and-i-have-both-reasons-and-an-alternative-named-vulmak?p=1559884#post1559884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The more things remain the same, the more they change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most people are very happy with Lunars, so it doesn't tend to repeatedly come up in completely unrelated topics apropos of nothing.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-12T17:49:30-07:00","id":1559907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1559861-i-hate-minister-mog-and-i-have-both-reasons-and-an-alternative-named-vulmak?p=1559905#post1559905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most people are very happy with Lunars, so it doesn't tend to repeatedly come up in completely unrelated topics apropos of nothing.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>How much talk about Exalted even actually happens nowadays? Certainly not much on this forum, or rpg.net, and frequently not even on Sword of Creation, given the post dates and time between posts, frequently for weeks on end. Hype managed to get the last few hardbacks some eyes on them during the campaign, but that tends to die down not too long after the campaign (and a fair bit of the noise for Infernals was someone oddly afraid that they would get changed into something unrecognizable from 2e and that they would be ruined forever and that Sidereals would become better wielders of Yozi power and...).<br /> <br /> Lunars happened really, really early into the cycle. Even without other considerations, it's showing its age being closer to the long since abandoned writing of the core than to Abyssals, which re-tuned a lot of what Lunars were probably using as balance points. Just look at how Lunars have to buy an entire Charm to refill flame weapons with their ammo-production Charm; just about every other type of Chosen does that as a component of a more prominent Charm. Abyssals and Alchemicals have Essence 1 Charms to inflict agg on anyone they hit and not on single &quot;enemy&quot; types, making a lack of it in Lunars look pretty odd, honestly. It's not even like it would be athematic for them; they can permakill gods, too. However much people might like what they have now, it's natural to see the progress other Charm sets made, look at what else has been done, and say &quot;We could do better.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T02:43:09-07:00","id":1559917,"title":"","content":"Nowadays, most of the chatter is on the discord.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T10:55:15-07:00","id":1559925,"title":"","content":"So I think a key thing about the Divine Ministers is that their utility as aspects of Authochthon is secondary to what they represent to Authochthonian society. What they provide as figures of veneration, and part of the system of values for the Octet. In that case, I think the great value of Mog is that he represents divine validation of the Octet's stifling orthodoxy. That there's a common model for what their society and their faith should be, and anything that deviates from that should be treated with the greatest harshness.<br /> <br /> Of course, as Authochthonia has developed, there's been a lot more variation and nuance to the structure of their societies, and that's the thing that introduces a lot of tension with a deity such as Mog. Not least because one could write it as ambiguous even within himself what the specifics of orthodoxy are or ought to be. It probably helps that one can play him in terms of being more invested in <i>something</i> being a common orthodoxy, rather than the fine details of it. The important thing is a standard to which everybody must adhere.<br /> <br /> Now a person doesn't necessarily need to respect that if they want to make their own custom Divine Minister, but I think they at least need to consider the relevance of removing it and what doing so changes about the Eight Nations. <br /> <br /> I feel as though this Divine Minister of the SOP as currently written removes some of the grit and spirituality from the make up of Autochthonian religion. Even for its own concept, it feels like a take on the Great Maker and the world within him that is very technically oriented, that lines too much on the idea of him as an industrial being and leaves out the sense that he's an entity for whom Faith and Doctrine are among his favourite inventions.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, I would dispute the idea that there's a fault in Mog as a source of dogma when he can provide direct divine insight. Dogma and divine revelation aren't mutually contradictory ideas, they're nested concepts. Indeed, much real world dogma is founded on the assertion that it is derived from revelation.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T11:03:51-07:00","id":1559926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1559861-i-hate-minister-mog-and-i-have-both-reasons-and-an-alternative-named-vulmak?p=1559876#post1559876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But where do you see Mog emerging in the timeline of souls that I described? Or do you see anything inaccurate in my proposed timeline of Autocthon's personal growth?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really sure it makes sense for Primordials to give a general impression of their souls developing one at a time. But to the extent of it as a framing, I could imagine the yearning for stability, as something in tension with his overall dynamic drive to create and innovate and explore, as coming somewhere at a point where an abundance of changes became overwhelming to his attentions or efforts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T14:28:51-07:00","id":1559934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yue Ryong</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1559861-i-hate-minister-mog-and-i-have-both-reasons-and-an-alternative-named-vulmak?p=1559917#post1559917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nowadays, most of the chatter is on the discord.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my theory.<br /> <br /> But I don't like using Discord.<br /> <br /> I don't like Reddit, either, but I can tolerate Reddit more than Discord.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T17:36:15-07:00","id":1559938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1559861-i-hate-minister-mog-and-i-have-both-reasons-and-an-alternative-named-vulmak?p=1559934#post1559934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's my theory.<br /> <br /> But I don't like using Discord.<br /> <br /> I don't like Reddit, either, but I can tolerate Reddit more than Discord.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not even sure when it would be good to go on if I had Discord. Most chat rooms I've been on seem to be most active when I'm off doing something else (usually, exercising or asleep). I keep tabs on the Exalted subreddit, but fear actually getting a login on account of how I would almost certainly get sucked into yet more acrimonious W5 conversations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}